{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "root": {
    "type": "Grid",
    "props": {
      "columns": 12,
      "gap": 16
    },
    "children": [
      {
        "type": "Card",
        "id": "summary_card",
        "props": {
          "span": 12,
          "variant": "hero"
        },
        "data": {
          "dataset": "summary"
        },
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "KPIStrip",
            "id": "summary_kpi",
            "props": {
              "items": [
                {
                  "label": "Formulas",
                  "field": "finding_count",
                  "format": "number"
                },
                {
                  "label": "Placeholders",
                  "field": "placeholders",
                  "format": "number"
                },
                {
                  "label": "Affected objects",
                  "field": "affected_objects",
                  "format": "number"
                },
                {
                  "label": "Affected files",
                  "field": "affected_files",
                  "format": "number"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "Card",
        "id": "findings_card",
        "props": {
          "span": 12,
          "title": "Formulas with <Function Missing>"
        },
        "data": {
          "dataset": "findings"
        },
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "Table",
            "id": "findings_table",
            "props": {
              "rowKey": "row_key",
              "density": "comfortable",
              "sortable": true,
              "searchable": "auto",
              "searchAutoThreshold": 3,
              "searchPlaceholder": "Search file, object or formula…",
              "columns": [
                {
                  "field": "file",
                  "label": "File"
                },
                {
                  "field": "name",
                  "label": "Object"
                },
                {
                  "field": "type",
                  "label": "Type",
                  "format": "badge"
                },
                {
                  "field": "calc_role",
                  "label": "Calculation"
                },
                {
                  "field": "step_no",
                  "label": "Step",
                  "align": "right",
                  "format": "number"
                },
                {
                  "field": "missing_count",
                  "label": "Missing",
                  "align": "right",
                  "format": "number"
                },
                {
                  "field": "formula_excerpt",
                  "label": "Formula"
                }
              ],
              "onRowClick": {
                "action": "openObject",
                "args": {
                  "uuid": "{{nav_uuid}}",
                  "type": "{{type}}",
                  "file": "{{file}}",
                  "step": "{{step_uuid}}",
                  "marks": "{{marks}}",
                  "ref_src": "plugin_function_missing_export",
                  "ref_msgid": "function-missing"
                }
              },
              "empty": {
                "message": "No formula lost a plug-in function at export time."
              },
              "alwaysShowCount": true
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "Card",
        "id": "notes_card",
        "props": {
          "span": 12,
          "title": "About this check"
        },
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "Markdown",
            "id": "notes_md",
            "props": {
              "content": "When a plug-in is **not loaded on the client that saves the XML**, FileMaker replaces the function name in the formula text itself with the placeholder `<Function Missing>` (and tags the DDR chunk as an unresolvable reference). The call is gone from the export: no plug-in object, no call edge — and the text no longer says which plug-in it was. The rule reads the formula **text**, so it works with and without DDR info.\n\n**No fix inside FM-Lab.** Save the file as XML again on a client with the plug-in installed and enabled. The *formula excerpt* keeps the arguments — often the only hint which plug-in is meant.\n\nThe import log reports the same defect as a warning (`Function Missing` chunks)."
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
